e could not have caught this), but the gripper actually closed on and lifted u_orange, an inactive neighboring part, while u_brown was never touched. This is a direct violation of the missed-grasp effect (grasp must close on the commanded part and not another) and simultaneously violates the standing undisturbed-objects invariant over u_orange, which was not due to be acted on in this step. The in-hand-slippage fire on u_brown is a consequence of the same root cause, not an independent slip: u_brown was never grasped, so \"while held\" never became true, and the relative-frame departure merely reflects u_brown sitting still while the tcp (now carrying u_orange) moved away."},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":28}
